e image content may be slightly different from reality at the points where multiple images were combined. This manipulation is often required due to lens, perspective, and parallax distortions."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2015-07-28"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Rftblr\" title=\"User:Rftblr\">Robert F. Tobler</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":60325982,"title":"File:Tokyo Metro and JR East at Ochanomizu, Tokyo.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Tokyo_Metro_and_JR_East_at_Ochanomizu%2C_Tokyo.jpg/960px-Tokyo_Metro_and_JR_East_at_Ochanomizu%2C_Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tokyo_Metro_and_JR_East_at_Ochanomizu,_Tokyo.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Tokyo Metro 02 series nr. 618 (below) on the Marunouchi Line crosses the Kanda river, while, above, a E233 set of JR East on the Chuo main line just leaves Ochanomizu. If you look closely, you can also spot a E231 set of JR east on the Sobu line, behind the platform. Photo taken at Ochanomizu, Tokyo, Japan."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2017-05-01 16:57:07"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Kabelleger\" title=\"User:Kabelleger\">Kabelleger / David Gubler</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":74257936,"title":"File:Tokyo Shibuya Scramble Crossing 2018-10-09.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/960px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Pedestrians crossing perhaps the most famous scramble i